From e845078963d0a99314fbfaadf30fc5b04f9f034f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:57:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The costume room's other five: 307 things to put away

The costume room shipped with one working piece of furniture. The treasure chest held your clue
rewards; the cape rack, the magic wardrobe, the armour case, the toy box and the fancy dress box
were five hotspots with a Build op and nothing behind it. Building them is what this is.

ONE MECHANISM, FIVE SPACES. The chest already does storage the way this repo does storage - a perm
inv and a chat menu, no new interface, the same shape as the herb sack and the looting bag. These
five are that again, so rather than five near-copies of poh_costume.rs2 there is one set of procs
in poh_stores.rs2 and a store index that picks which run of the item list a click may see. An inv
cannot be handed to a proc - nothing in the repo does it and the engine's own commands are where
the type appears - so all five share poh_store_inv and each owns a contiguous run of it.
poh_store_first/_last is that run, poh_store_setfirst/_setlast the sets inside it, and the index
into poh_store_item is also the slot, so nothing has to search.

WHAT GOES IN THEM was the real work, and it is derived rather than remembered. Every name is
checked against pack/obj.pack, against the treasure chest's own 72, and against the other four
stores before the generator writes anything - four items turned out to be clue rewards the chest
already holds (the three berets and the highwayman mask) and came out of the fancy dress box for
it. 307 items in 47 sets: 87 capes and hoods, 58 robes and staves, 53 pieces of armour, 37 toys,
72 costume pieces.

THE ART is a rev-474 import of its own, 38 locs and 41 models, in poh_costume_storage.loc. The
build levels are OSRS's own - 54 to 99, 42 to 96, 46 to 82, 50 to 86, 44 to 80 - and the top of
the cape rack costs one magic stone, which is why the Stonemason in Keldagrim now stocks them at
OSRS's own 4,000,000. Its cache cost is twice that, because a shop charges cost x multiplier /
1000 and ^poh_stone_sell is 500: the same arithmetic that makes the marble block 125,000.

THE FIVE FAMILIES ARE APPENDED, not inserted. A family's position in furnspec.json is its id and
an item's position is the number written into a player's saved furniture, so putting them beside
the treasure chest where they read best renumbered 292 existing items and quietly rearranged every
house already standing. They go on the end.

The same rule is why this sits above the Max cape round rather than under it. Both rounds append
to pack/obj.pack and pack/model.pack, and the first cut of this one claimed obj 8312 for the magic
stone and models 16234 up - ids the Max cape and the elder chaos robes had already taken. The
magic stone is 8317 now and the costume art runs 16265 to 16305. Nothing else collided:
loc.pack, inv.pack and varp.pack were clear, and varp 1169 is the Max cape's alone.

Battery group 62 re-derives all of it: the lists against the objs, against the chest and against
each other; the five windows tiling the item list with no gap and no overlap; the sets tiling each
store's own run; the capacities against the furniture; the footprints against the hotspots; and
every emitted trigger opening its own store at its own item number. Twenty mutations, all red.

Two of them were red for the wrong reason first time and found real holes:

  - poh_furn_ops.rs2 was not in group 38's compare list, and had not been since it was split out.
    That group re-runs genfurn IN PLACE, so a hand-edit to it - a cape rack rewired to open the
    magic wardrobe's storage - was regenerated away and the battery came out green. Every trigger
    in the build lives in that file. It is in the list now.
  - the check on "More sets..." wrapping to its own store's first set passed on a proc that wrapped
    to set 0, because it only looked for the table name. It reads the assignment now.

Dead Build ops in a house: 37 -> 32. What is left is the three Hedging spaces and 29 in dungeon
and upper-floor zones that need a storey this build does not have yet.

